 zinc and hydrochloric acid to give the corresponding\nhydrocarbon? ","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Ethyl acetate "},{"identifier":"B","content":"Butan -2-one "},{"identifier":"C","content":"Acetamide"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Acetic acid"}],"correct_options":["B"],"answer":null,"explanation":"It is Clemmensen's reduction\n<br><br><img class=\"question-image\" src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/cH3ojeIoLIghZMg9W/5p9M0embFtExfGDEp6Mxd8XSlFrH4/WaUTpIL7xX3PjFdGymdlsT/image.png\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"AIEEE 2004 Chemistry - Aldehydes, Ketones and Carboxylic Acids Question 278 English Explanation\"> "}},"permalink":"which-one-of-the-following-reduced-with-zinc-and-hydrochlori-2004-marks-4-0bv6dpfm7zdrqnd5.htm","timeAllotted":120000,"paperId":"aieee-2004","topic":"chemical-reactions-for-aldehydes-and-ketones","isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":[],"yearKey":"aieee-2004","active":true},{"country":"in","examGroup":"jee","question_id":"BZ38P7EdQ4ozjTng","exam":"jee-main","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"subjectGroup":null,"subject":"chemistry","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","languages":["en"],"chapter":"coordination-compounds","year":2004,"paperTitle":"AIEEE 2004","difficulty":"easy","topicName":null,"type":"mcq","examDate":null,"question":{"en":{"content":"The coordination number of central metal atom in a complex is determined by :","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"the number of ligands around a metal ion bonded by sigma bonds"},{"identifier":"B","content":"the number of only anionic ligands bonded to the metal ion"},{"identifier":"C","content":"the number of ligands around a metal ion bonded by sigma and pi- bonds both "},{"identifier":"D","content":"the number of ligands around a metal ion bonded by pi-bonds"}],"correct_options":["A"],"answer":null,"explanation":"The coordination number of central metal atom in a complex is equal to number of monovalent ligands,  twice the number of bidentate ligands and so on, around the metal ion bonde